<Item XName="EquationText" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>% this DPD model negates the normalized AMAM and AMPM data&#x000D;&#x000A;% to use it as a correction factor to return to linear Pin-Pout&#x000D;&#x000A;% Also note that since this power table is input-referred, we&#x000D;&#x000A;% do not need to remove the nominal gain = 18.535.&#x000D;&#x000A;%&#x000D;&#x000A;thisPowerDBM=30+10*log10((abs(input)).^2/(2*Rref));&#x000D;&#x000A;LUTmin=min(Pdata);&#x000D;&#x000A;LUTmax=max(Pdata);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%&#x000D;&#x000A;% if you do gain Expansion, then you are moving farther up the &#x000D;&#x000A;% amplifier compression.  Look ahead to that level, and make a &#x000D;&#x000A;% first-order correction with even more expansion.  There are &#x000D;&#x000A;% several ways to control extrapolation for modulated signals; &#x000D;&#x000A;% in this case we will brute-force limit the values to what&apos;s &#x000D;&#x000A;% within the power range of the lookup table.&#x000D;&#x000A;%&#x000D;&#x000A;if (thisPowerDBM&gt;LUTmax) &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x0009;thisPowerDBM=LUTmax;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;if (thisPowerDBM&lt;LUTmin) &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x0009;thisPowerDBM=LUTmin;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;gainExpand=-interp1(Pdata,Gdata,thisPowerDBM,&apos;linear&apos;,&apos;extrap&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;overshotDBM=thisPowerDBM+gainExpand;&#x000D;&#x000A;if (overshotDBM&gt;LUTmax) &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x0009;overshotDBM=LUTmax;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;if (overshotDBM&lt;LUTmin) &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x0009;overshotDBM=LUTmin;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;gainDB=-interp1(Pdata,Gdata,overshotDBM,&apos;linear&apos;,&apos;extrap&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;%&#x000D;&#x000A;% once you have the power level, you don&apos;t need to iterate for phase.&#x000D;&#x000A;phaseRAD=-interp1(Pdata,Adata,overshotDBM,&apos;linear&apos;,&apos;extrap&apos;)*pi/180;&#x000D;&#x000A;gainpolar=10^(gainDB/20)*exp(i*phaseRAD);&#x000D;&#x000A;if (abs(enable) &gt; 0.999)&#x000D;&#x000A;   outvar=input*gainpolar;&#x000D;&#x000A;else&#x000D;&#x000A;   outvar=input;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;output=outvar;&#x000D;&#x000A;</DataEntry>
