<Item XName="ReadMe" UserName="ReadMe" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=6&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Modeling PA Compression&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This example models a 2140MHz&amp;nbsp;basestation amplifier&amp;nbsp;designed in ADS using a Freescale FET.&amp;nbsp; The ADS microstrip circuit was extracted to an X-parameter file, as well as various power-dependent parameters exported from DataDisplay to a CSV file.&amp;nbsp; There are a few ways to import the data and model amplifiers.&amp;nbsp; The X-parameter case is then used in a RFLINK beamforming situation.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;X-parameter amplifier extracted from ADS &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;use Spectrasys, which can then be used in RF LINK.&amp;nbsp; Direct method.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Absolute power&amp;nbsp;curves from ADS --&amp;gt;CSV file--&amp;gt; workspace variables&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;using interpolated math Lookup table.&amp;nbsp; Flexible, but slow.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;AMAM/AMPM compression curves from ADS --&amp;gt; CSV file &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;using &quot;Amplifier&quot; distortion model.&amp;nbsp; The fastest execution.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Methods not shown:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;direct co-sim with ADS Ptolemy/CktEnvelope&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;export an FCE model from GoldenGate&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;measure an X-parameter on a PNA-X analyzer&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;capture power-dependent AMAM, AMPM using a modulated &lt;BR&gt;signal on the VSG/VSA, and the 89600 VSA software.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;SystemVue&apos;s own W1716 DPD, a more professional tool &lt;BR&gt;for linearization that can correct for memory effects.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Here, since you are modeling a PA&amp;nbsp;using a power compression curve, you are only&amp;nbsp;a couple steps away from having a simple DPD correction model.&amp;nbsp; This workspace provides a couple possible ways to approximate that.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
